<title>GERMANY: Hanover Re sees only small cost from floods.</title>
<headline>Hanover Re sees only small cost from floods.</headline>
<dateline>HANNOVER, Germany 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>German reinsurer Hannover Rueck said on Monday it did not expect to sustain huge costs as a result of the flood wave which has hit Poland, the Czech Republic and east Germany.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman said the claims from the Czech Republic were expected to be the highest, running to more than 10 million marks, but that these were borne in part by another reinsurer. This meant the total for Hanover Re would be under 10 million marks.</p>
<p>Costs of around five million marks were expected from Poland and less than one million marks from east Germany, the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
